From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 14:59:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: bounds-check an image atomic

Metal bounds-checks a texture read and discards an out of range texture
write, so a KosmicKrisp storage image gets robustImageAccess2 semantics
from the hardware and the driver never had to guard an image access. A
texture atomic is not covered by that: an out of range coordinate turns
into an address outside the texture, and the access can reach memory the
submission does not own instead of being dropped.

Guard the two image atomic intrinsics with nir_lower_robust_access, which
rejects the coordinate against the image size and yields zero for the
out of range case, exactly as robustImageAccess2 requires. It runs before
descriptor lowering so the size query is still an image deref that pass
resolves, and so the comparison uses the Vulkan coordinate space, before
the cube and 1D rewrites fold a face or a layer into it.

Reads and writes stay unguarded here: the hardware already covers them
within a texture's bounds, descriptor lowering checks a texel buffer
coordinate against its view before moving it into the wider texture Metal
needs, and a size query per access is not free.
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
index 95605adc464b416be9f6a530a222b13866e3434d..a21e498b39e07ad0a3421107cda0654de53990db 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
@@ -1300,6 +1300,26 @@ kk_lower_fs(struct kk_device *dev, nir_shader *nir,
    }
 }
 
+/* Which accesses nir_lower_robust_access has to guard for us.  Metal already
+ * gives a texture read and a texture write robustImageAccess2 behaviour
+ * within the texture's own bounds, descriptor lowering rejects a texel buffer
+ * coordinate outside its view before moving it into the wider texture that
+ * starts in front of the view, and buffer robustness arrives with the address
+ * format, so only an image atomic is left unguarded.
+ */
+static bool
+kk_image_atomic_needs_bounds(const nir_intrinsic_instr *intr,
+                             UNUSED const void *data)
+{
+   switch (intr->intrinsic) {
+   case nir_intrinsic_image_deref_atomic:
+   case nir_intrinsic_image_deref_atomic_swap:
+      return true;
+   default:
+      return false;
+   }
+}
+
 static void
 kk_lower_nir(struct kk_device *dev, nir_shader *nir, bool emulated_stage,
              bool pipeline_statistics,
@@ -1415,6 +1435,19 @@ kk_lower_nir(struct kk_device *dev, nir_shader *nir, bool emulated_stage,
       kk_lower_fs(dev, nir, state, writes_depth, pipeline_statistics);
    }
 
+   /* Metal bounds-checks a texture read and discards an out of range texture
+    * write, so those carry robustImageAccess2 semantics for free.  A texture
+    * atomic does not: an out of range coordinate reaches memory outside the
+    * texture, and on some GPUs that access never completes.  Reject the
+    * coordinate before the atomic issues instead.
+    *
+    * This runs before descriptor lowering so the size query is still an image
+    * deref that pass resolves, and so the comparison happens in the Vulkan
+    * coordinate space, before the cube and 1D rewrites move it.
+    */
+   NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_robust_access, kk_image_atomic_needs_bounds,
+            NULL);
+
    /* Descriptor lowering needs to happen after lowering blend since we will
     * generate a nir_intrinsic_load_blend_const_color_rgba which gets lowered by
     * the lower descriptor pass
